    <title>
      <narrative xml:lang="en">NESA Center Morocco - Algeria Task Force 01-23</narrative>
    </title>
    <description type="1">
      <narrative xml:lang="en">The Algerian-Moroccan Task Force, organized by the Near East South Asia Center for Strategic Studies (NESA) in partnership with USAFRICOM. This program is a test-pilot program only designed to provide an opportunity for Algerians and Moroccans to come together in an informal, candid and constructive way to address common concerns and pressing issues between the two countries. The pilot will evaluate the constructiveness of a TF series by having participants start the process addressing two basic questions: What do you want to see in Morocco and Algeria? and Where are there opportunities for cooperation/collaboration? The Alg-Mor only intense RT discussion on 19 Feb follows 2 days (20-24 hrs) of broader security discussions. The meeting will be held under Chatham House Rule, by-name invitation only.</narrative>
    </description>
